🍴 STEP 1: Fork the Repository
👉 Go to the repository on GitHub
👉 Click Fork (top right)
This creates your own copy of the project

📥 STEP 2: Clone Your Fork
git clone https://github.com/YOUR-USERNAME/REPO-NAME.git

👉 This downloads the project to your computer

📂 STEP 3: Go Inside the Folder
cd REPO-NAME

👉 Moves you into the project directory

✍️ STEP 4: Make Changes
👉 Open the folder in VS Code
👉 Add your card in index.html

🔍 STEP 5: Check Changes
git status

👉 Shows what files you changed

➕ STEP 6: Add Changes
git add .

👉 Stages all your changes for commit

📝 STEP 7: Commit Changes
git commit -m "Added my first PR 🎉"

👉 Saves your changes with a message


🚀 STEP 8: Push to GitHub
git push origin main

👉 Uploads your code to your GitHub fork

🔁 STEP 9: Create Pull Request
👉 Go to your fork on GitHub
👉 Click Compare & Pull Request
👉 Click Create Pull Request
👉 Done 🎉

⚠️ COMMON ERRORS (DON’T PANIC)

 Error: “Permission denied”
👉 Solution:
Use your GitHub username
Use Personal Access Token instead of password

 Error: “Nothing to commit”
👉 Means:
You didn’t change anything
👉 Solution:
Make sure you edited the file

 Error: “Rejected (fetch first)”
👉 Solution:
git pull origin main --allow-unrelated-histories

Then push again:
git push origin main

